On May 1, 7:25 am, Matt Frisch <matus...@yahoo.spam.me.not.com> wrote:

> Hell, I spend most of the entire GAME burdened, why would the ascension be
> any different?

One word: Pestilence.

I go through most of my games burdened too, but because of that nasty
guy I do try to shed weight at the level one upstairs. I don't always
succeed in reaching unburdened status, but I breathe easier if I do.
Because the only other creature in vanilla NH that can kill you
outright that quickly is Demogorgon, and he's not guaranteed to
appear. (OK, Juiblex causes fatal illness also of course, but he's so
easy to kill you have plenty of time to cure yourself even if he does
swallow you, and, unlike Pestilence, he doesn't regenerate.)

> All the other artifacts found in the game, including the three invocation
> relics, and create sting/orcrist right before hitting the planes. Plus if
> any archons spawn, you kill them for their guaranteed drops of Demonbane
> and the Sunsword (presuming you didn't already have those), all the
> valuable gems, the nazgul rings, every amulet you found, a dozen potions of
> holy water (instead of remove curse scrolls, I've never found any use for
> those in the endgame, holy water is nice though), and 14-20 MORE k-rats
> than you bring.

I understand the urge to collect, especially with artifacts, though I
don't bother with most of them myself. But for score, you should
really not bother with amulets; many of the gems are much lighter
weight for more value. And the cheap plastic Yendor imitations are
worth *nothing*!

As far as food, I prefer the ring of slow digestion, though I'll swap
that for levitation and free action on all planes after Earth, and for
conflict and free action on Astral. Though I might bring a half-dozen
K rations along and a few more in my BoH, I don't think I've ever
needed more than one or two of them to get me through the endgame...

